IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc19-s492-27-to-3.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, ss 492.27 to 492.3, Days to Be Excluded (text lines 10999-11019), in PART XV.1 Unreasonable Delay.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website
-- consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- The three sections 492.27, 492.28 and 492.29 open with the same words: "Subject to section 492.3, in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall not
-- take into account any day within ..." (the periods listed). That chapeau is one function (named for s 492.27, citing all three); each limb is a function that composes the chapeau with the
-- limb's own period. Each function is asked of ONE day.
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN. For the bar, JUST TRUE = "the court shall not take the day into account"; JUST FALSE = this limb does not bar it (the "In determining" gate, the "if" late-filing
-- gate or the period is not met: rule of 2026-10-29 (a) and ruling of 2026-11-05 (a), (b)); NOTHING = not covered (a list the text does not close; "subject to section 492.3"; a case outside the limb's scope).
-- Dates are `Date day month year`. "at least 60 days before the hearing" is computed with `Day` (a day count of a date); a period that "begins on the day" and "ends on the day" takes both end days in (fork F10).

§ `s 492.27 -- exclusions for sexual offence proceedings: the chapeau, shared by ss 492.27, 492.28 and 492.29`

-- The chapeau: the court shall not take into account any day within the period the section lists, "Subject to section 492.3", "in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay".
-- Inputs: whether the court is determining that question; the answer of s 492.3 (a seam inside this module: only JUST TRUE changes the outcome); and whether the day is within the limb's period.
-- Order: the "In determining" gate first; then the period (outside it the section says no); then "Subject to section 492.3": when s 492.3 applies, the text says only that the court takes the action into account
-- in determining the days, and does not say what days then remain, so the answer is NOT COVERED (fork F9).
-- src:11001 | 492.27 Subject to section 492.3, in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall not take into account any day within any of the following periods:
@ref Criminal Code ss 492.27, 492.28 and 492.29, chapeau (src:11001)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the day is within a period that the limb lists` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay"
    ELSE CONSIDER `the day is within a period that the limb lists`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any day within any of the following periods"
         WHEN JUST within THEN
             IF NOT (within)
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any day within any of the following periods"
             ELSE CONSIDER `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith`
                  WHEN JUST applies THEN
                      IF applies
                      THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 492.3"
                      ELSE JUST TRUE
                  OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The chapeau as a regulative rule: the court SHANT take the day into account where the limb's bar answers JUST TRUE; otherwise nothing is owed. The text gives no period, so there is no WITHIN.
@ref Criminal Code ss 492.27, 492.28 and 492.29, chapeau (src:11001)
DECLARE `s 492.27 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.27 take the day into account in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`

@ref Criminal Code ss 492.27, 492.28 and 492.29, chapeau (src:11001)
GIVEN `the answer of the limb: the court shall not take the day into account` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.27 act`
`s 492.27 the prohibition on the court taking the day into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of the limb: the court shall not take the day into account`
    WHEN JUST barred THEN
        IF barred
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             SHANT `s 492.27 take the day into account in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "ss 492.27 to 492.29: the court took into account a day it shall not take into account in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

-- A day it took, or a period attributable: the two kinds of day in (i) and (ii) of each limb. (i) "the period that consists of the cumulative number of days it took to hear the application";
-- (ii) "any other period, as determined by the court, that is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed [served] ... at least 60 days before the hearing, including any delay
-- caused by the adjournment of any proceeding that is attributable to the late filing of the application". (ii) hands the judgment to the court, so the caller says whether the court has so determined
-- (that is the constructor; fork F6). A day that is in neither: the list of periods is not closed with "only", so NOT COVERED. The same three constructors serve (a), (b) and (c).
-- src:11002 | (a) in respect of any application made under section 276.01, if a copy of the application was not filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in section 276.02,
-- src:11003 | (i) the period that consists of the cumulative number of days it took to hear the application, and
-- src:11004 | (ii) any other period, as determined by the court, that is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing, including any delay caused by the adjournment of any proceeding that is attributable to the late filing of the application;
@ref Criminal Code s 492.27(a), (a)(i), (a)(ii) (src:11002-11004)
DECLARE `s 492.27 kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application`
    `s 492.27(ii) a day in another period that the court has determined is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed or served at least 60 days before the hearing`
    `s 492.27 a day that is in neither period`

-- 60 days: "at least 60 days before the hearing" (paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)). A copy that was in place exactly 60 days before the hearing is "at least 60 days" before it (fork F7).
@ref Criminal Code s 492.27(a), (b) and (c) (src:11002-11004)
`s 492.27 sixty days` MEANS 60

-- Paragraph (a): was a copy of the application under section 276.01 filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in section 276.02?
-- JUST TRUE: yes, in time. JUST FALSE: no (never filed, or filed with someone who is the clerk of the court but too late, or filed with someone who is not the clerk): the "if" of paragraph (a) is met.
-- "clerk of the court" is a section 2 term ("includes a person ... who from time to time performs the duties of a clerk of the court"): the seam input is its answer, and a NOTHING from it is carried through.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.27(a) (src:11002)
GIVEN `the date a copy of the application was filed, if it was filed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `s 2 clerk of the court: the person with whom the copy was filed is the clerk of the court` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the date of the hearing referred to in section 276.02` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.27(a) a copy of the application was filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date a copy of the application was filed, if it was filed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "was not filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing"
    WHEN JUST filed THEN
        CONSIDER `s 2 clerk of the court: the person with whom the copy was filed is the clerk of the court`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "clerk of the court"
        WHEN JUST isclerk THEN
            IF isclerk
            THEN JUST (Day `the date of the hearing referred to in section 276.02` MINUS Day filed AT LEAST `s 492.27 sixty days`)
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "was not filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.27(a) (src:11002)
GIVEN `the copy was filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing, by s 492.27(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the kind of day` IS A `s 492.27 kind of day`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.27(a) the day is within a period of paragraph (a)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the copy was filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing, by s 492.27(a)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "clerk of the court"
    WHEN JUST inTime THEN
        IF inTime
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if a copy of the application was not filed with the clerk of the court at least 60 days before the hearing referred to in section 276.02"
        ELSE CONSIDER `the kind of day`
             WHEN `s 492.27(i) a day it took to hear the application` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 492.27(ii) a day in another period that the court has determined is attributable to the fact that a copy of the application was not filed or served at least 60 days before the hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `s 492.27 a day that is in neither period` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "any of the following periods"

@ref Criminal Code s 492.27(a) (src:11002-11004)
