§ `s 492.28 -- exclusions: the Canada Evidence Act`

-- A period "that begins on the day ... and ends on the day ... [finally determined]", asked of one day. Both end days are in the period (fork F10). A day before it begins or after it ends: outside a
-- period the text fixes in its own words, so JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)). Where the period has begun and is not yet ended (the end day is not known), a day on or after the beginning is NOT COVERED:
-- the text fixes the end by a day not yet arrived. This one helper serves paragraphs (a), (b) and (c) of s 492.28 and s 492.29, which are written in the same words.
-- src:11012 | 492.28 Subject to section 492.3, in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall not take into account any day within any of the following periods:
-- src:11013 | (a) in the case of an objection made under subsection 37(1) of the Canada Evidence Act before a superior court, the period that begins on the day the objection was made and ends on the day the objection was finally determined;
-- src:11014 | (b) in the case where an objection was made under subsection 37(1) of that Act before a court, person or body other than a superior court and an application was made under subsection 37(3) of that Act in respect of the objection, the period that begins on the day the objection was made and ends on the day the application was finally determined;
-- src:11015 | (c) in the case of an application made under subsection 38.04(1) or (2) of that Act in respect of a notice arising from the prosecution of the offence given under any of subsections 38.01(1) to (4) of that Act, the period that begins on the day the application was made and ends on the day the application was finally determined.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.28(a), (b), (c) and s 492.29 (src:11012-11015)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the day the period begins` IS A DATE
      `the day the period ends, if it has ended` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.28 the day falls within the period that begins on one day and ends on another` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the period ends, if it has ended`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF day AT LEAST `the day the period begins`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "ends on the day the objection was finally determined"
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period that begins on the day"
    WHEN JUST ended THEN
        IF day AT LEAST `the day the period begins` AND day AT MOST ended
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the period that begins on the day"

-- Paragraph (a): "in the case of an objection made under subsection 37(1) of the Canada Evidence Act before a superior court": a scope ("in the case of": NOT COVERED outside it); the period runs from the day
-- the objection was made to the day it was finally determined.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.28(a) (src:11013)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the objection was made under subsection 37(1) of the Canada Evidence Act before a superior court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the objection was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the objection was finally determined, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.28(a) the court shall not take the day into account` MEANS
    `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3`
        `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
        `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith`
        (IF `the objection was made under subsection 37(1) of the Canada Evidence Act before a superior court`
         THEN `s 492.28 the day falls within the period that begins on one day and ends on another` day `the day the objection was made` `the day the objection was finally determined, if it has been`
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an objection made under subsection 37(1) of the Canada Evidence Act before a superior court"

-- Paragraph (b): "in the case where an objection was made under subsection 37(1) of that Act before a court, person or body other than a superior court and an application was made under subsection 37(3) of that
-- Act in respect of the objection": a "where" condition, so when it fails the answer is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); fork F11). The period runs from the day the objection was made to the day the APPLICATION was finally determined.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.28(b) (src:11014)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an objection was made under subsection 37(1) of that Act before a court, person or body other than a superior court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an application was made under subsection 37(3) of that Act in respect of the objection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the objection was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the application under subsection 37(3) was finally determined, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.28(b) the court shall not take the day into account` MEANS
    `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3`
        `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
        `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith`
        (IF `an objection was made under subsection 37(1) of that Act before a court, person or body other than a superior court` AND `an application was made under subsection 37(3) of that Act in respect of the objection`
         THEN `s 492.28 the day falls within the period that begins on one day and ends on another` day `the day the objection was made` `the day the application under subsection 37(3) was finally determined, if it has been`
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case where an objection was made under subsection 37(1) of that Act before a court, person or body other than a superior court and an application was made under subsection 37(3) of that Act in respect of the objection"

-- Paragraph (c): "in the case of an application made under subsection 38.04(1) or (2) of that Act in respect of a notice arising from the prosecution of the offence given under any of subsections 38.01(1) to (4)
-- of that Act": a scope ("in the case of": NOT COVERED outside it). The period runs from the day the application was made to the day it was finally determined.
