`s 492.28(c) the court shall not take the day into account` MEANS
    `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3`
        `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
        `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith`
        (IF `an application was made under subsection 38.04(1) or (2) of that Act in respect of a notice arising from the prosecution of the offence given under any of subsections 38.01(1) to (4) of that Act`
         THEN `s 492.28 the day falls within the period that begins on one day and ends on another` day `the day the application was made` `the day the application was finally determined, if it has been`
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an application made under subsection 38.04(1) or (2) of that Act"

§ `s 492.29 -- exclusion: the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act`

-- "the period that begins on the day any application under subsection 18.1(4) of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act was made and ends on the day it was finally determined". "any application" is the scope.
-- src:11017 | 492.29 Subject to section 492.3, in determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay, the court shall not take into account any day within the period that begins on the day any application under subsection 18.1(4) of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act was made and ends on the day it was finally determined.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.29 (src:11017)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application was made under subsection 18.1(4) of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the application was finally determined, if it has been` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.29 the court shall not take the day into account` MEANS
    `s 492.27 the court shall not take the day into account, subject to section 492.3`
        `the court is determining whether there has been or will be unreasonable delay`
        `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith`
        (IF `an application was made under subsection 18.1(4) of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act`
         THEN `s 492.28 the day falls within the period that begins on one day and ends on another` day `the day the application was made` `the day the application was finally determined, if it has been`
         ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any application under subsection 18.1(4) of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act"

§ `s 492.3 -- actions not made in good faith`

-- "For greater certainty, in determining the days that are not to be taken into account in relation to applications or objections referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29, the court shall take into account
-- any frivolous or dilatory action, or any action not made in good faith, taken by the prosecutor, by counsel representing the Attorney General of Canada or by any person acting on behalf of the prosecutor or
-- the Attorney General of Canada." A duty of the court. Gate: the determination of the days, in relation to such an application or objection (JUST FALSE if not). Then the action: frivolous, dilatory or not in good faith,
-- by one of the three named kinds of person. An action by anyone else, or one that is not frivolous, dilatory or in bad faith, is not named: NOT COVERED. What the court then does with the days is not stated (fork F9).
-- src:11019 | 492.3 For greater certainty, in determining the days that are not to be taken into account in relation to applications or objections referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29, the court shall take into account any frivolous or dilatory action, or any action not made in good faith, taken by the prosecutor, by counsel representing the Attorney General of Canada or by any person acting on behalf of the prosecutor or the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref Criminal Code s 492.3 (src:11019)
DECLARE `s 492.3 who took the action` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.3 the prosecutor`
    `s 492.3 counsel representing the Attorney General of Canada`
    `s 492.3 a person acting on behalf of the prosecutor or the Attorney General of Canada`
    `s 492.3 someone else`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.3 (src:11019)
GIVEN `the days being determined are days in relation to an application or objection referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is frivolous or dilatory, or is an action not made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who took the action` IS A `s 492.3 who took the action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the days being determined are days in relation to an application or objection referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in determining the days that are not to be taken into account in relation to applications or objections referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29"
        IF NOT (`the action is frivolous or dilatory, or is an action not made in good faith`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any frivolous or dilatory action, or any action not made in good faith"
        IF `who took the action` EQUALS `s 492.3 someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "taken by the prosecutor, by counsel representing the Attorney General of Canada or by any person acting on behalf of the prosecutor or the Attorney General of Canada"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref Criminal Code s 492.3 (src:11019)
DECLARE `s 492.3 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 492.3 take the action into account in determining the days that are not to be taken into account`

@ref Criminal Code s 492.3 (src:11019)
GIVEN `the days being determined are days in relation to an application or objection referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is frivolous or dilatory, or is an action not made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `who took the action` IS A `s 492.3 who took the action`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 492.3 act`
`s 492.3 the duty of the court to take the action into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 492.3: the court must take into account a frivolous or dilatory action or an action not made in good faith` `the days being determined are days in relation to an application or objection referred to in sections 492.27 to 492.29` `the action is frivolous or dilatory, or is an action not made in good faith` `who took the action`
    WHEN JUST owed THEN
        IF owed
        THEN PARTY `the court`
             MUST `s 492.3 take the action into account in determining the days that are not to be taken into account`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 492.3: the court did not take the action into account in determining the days that are not to be taken into account"
        ELSE FULFILLED
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED
